This folder is intentionally empty.

Project Zomboid's AdvancedAnimator walks <mod>/common/media/AnimSets,
<mod>/common/media/actiongroups, <mod>/42/media/AnimSets and
<mod>/42/media/actiongroups for EVERY loaded mod, on every Core.ResetLua.
A folder that does not exist makes its walkFileTree call visitFileFailed,
which logs a NoSuchFileException at Error severity - four per mod, every
reload. Benign, but it buries real errors in the DebugLog.

The folder existing is the entire fix. This file is only here because git
does not track empty directories.

Do NOT replace this with a placeholder .xml: searchFolders collects every
file ending in .xml (AdvancedAnimator.java:658-666) and the animation
loader then tries to parse it, which trades a harmless log line for a real
one. Any other extension is ignored.

The name carries the mod id and the tier because ZomboidFileSystem.loadMod
maps common/ and <version>/ into ONE relative namespace and logs
'mod "X" overrides <rel>' whenever two files land on the same relative path
(ZomboidFileSystem.java:620-621). A plain .keep in all fourteen mods would
silence 56 errors and create 26 override lines.
